{
  "$readme": [
    "One contract, three readers.",
    "",
    "Publishing a nasheed can take two roads: through the `publish` Edge Function, whose",
    "validator is supabase/functions/_shared/validate.ts, or straight from the browser to",
    "PostgREST, whose validator is src/lib/wire.ts. They are hand-written mirrors of each",
    "other, and a mirror that drifts is worse than no mirror at all — the same form would",
    "be accepted one day and refused the next, depending on whether a function is deployed.",
    "",
    "So both are run against these cases and must agree, and every `row` here is also",
    "inserted into a real Postgres by scripts/pg-test.mjs, which is what proves the",
    "validators produce something the table's check constraints actually accept.",
    "",
    "  deno test supabase/functions/_shared/contract_test.ts   the function's validator",
    "  npm run contract:test                                   the browser's mirror",
    "  npm run sql:test                                        and the database itself",
    "",
    "A case is either { input, row } — the payload validates to exactly this row — or",
    "{ input, error: { status, field, says } } — it is refused, with this status, this",
    "field for the form to highlight, and this much of the sentence it says.",
    "",
    "Rules mirrored here, all of which are also CHECK constraints on public.songs:",
    "title 2–120 · note ≤ 480 · maqam in the ten names · root 24–96 · bpm 30–240 ·",
    "voices solo|duet|choir · duff null or ^[DT.]{16}$ · duff_enter intro|verse ·",
    "passes 1–6 · accent jade|gold|turq|madder|cobalt · year null or 600–2200 ·",
    "tags ≤ 8, lowercased, ≤ 24 chars · lines 0–40 · duration_ms null or 1000–86400000 ·",
    "audio ≤ 60 MB · artwork ≤ 8 MB · storage paths inside the publisher's own folder."
  ],
